{
  "dom_id": "step-q184240",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Prove that  $3n-1$ is even whenever $n$ is odd.\n\nIf $n$ is odd, then $n=\\,${{field-1}} for {{field-2}}.\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-1 & ={{field-3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ {{field-4}}. Since $a$ is {{field-5}}, we have that $b$ is {{field-6}}.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-1 & ={{field-7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $3n-1$ is {{field-8}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Recall the following:\n\n- If an integer $n$ is even, then there exists an integer $p$ such that $n=2p.$\n\n- If an integer $n$ is odd, then there exists an integer $q$ such that $n=2q+1.$\n\nIn this case, we need to prove the following:\n\n$$\nn\\text{ is odd}\\,⇒\\,3n-1\\text{ is even}\n$$\n\nWe start by using the fact that $n$ is odd.\n\nIf $n$ is odd, then $n=2a+1$ for some integer $a.$\n\nThe idea is to substitute $n=2a+1$ into the expression $3n-1$ and show it is even by writing it as a multiple of $2.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-1 & =3(2a+1)-1 \\\\  & =6a+3-1 \\\\  & =6a+2 \\\\  & =2{{(3a+1)}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we define another integer $b=3a+1$ (highlighted above), we have that $3n-1=2b,$ which shows that $3n-1$ is indeed a multiple of $2.$\n\nLet $b=3a+1.$ Since $a$ is an integer, we have that $b$ is an integer. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-1 & =2{{(3a+1)}_{⏟}}_{b} \\\\  & =2b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$\n\nFinally, we write our conclusion.\n\nTherefore, $3n-1$ is even.\n\nPROOF\n\nIf $n$ is odd, then $n=\\,$$2a+1$ for some integer $a$.\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-1 & =2(3a+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ $3a+1$. Since $a$ is an integer, we have that $b$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-1 & =2b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $3n-1$ is even.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
